## 2. Host System Preparation

### 2.1 Host Dependencies
Building a custom Linux distribution with Yocto requires a modern Linux host (Ubuntu 22.04/24.04 LTS or Debian 12 recommended) with at least **8 CPU cores**, **16 GB RAM**, and **100 GB free disk space**.

Install the mandatory host packages:

```bash
sudo apt update && sudo apt install -y \
    gawk wget git diffstat unzip texinfo gcc build-essential \
    chrpath socat cpio python3 python3-pip python3-pexpect \
    xz-utils debianutils iputils-ping python3-git python3-jinja2 \
    libegl1-mesa libsdl1.2-dev pylint xterm python3-subunit \
    mesa-common-dev zstd liblz4-tool bmap-tools file locales
```

Configure host locale to UTF-8 (mandatory for BitBake sanity checks):

```bash
sudo locale-gen en_US.UTF-8
export LANG=en_US.UTF-8
export LC_ALL=en_US.UTF-8
```

### 2.2 Git Buffer Configuration
Prevent connection drops and HTTP transfer timeouts during large upstream repository fetches (such as the Linux kernel and GCC toolchains):

```bash
git config --global http.postBuffer 524288000
git config --global core.compression 0
```

