## 3. Workspace Setup & Layer Fetching

Create a dedicated workspace directory and clone the Poky reference distribution alongside the necessary Board Support Package (BSP) and utility layers matching the `scarthgap` LTS branch.

```bash
# Create main workspace directory
mkdir -p ~/rpi-yocto
cd ~/rpi-yocto

# Clone Poky Reference System (Scarthgap LTS)
git clone -b scarthgap git://git.yoctoproject.org/poky.git poky

# Clone Raspberry Pi Hardware BSP Layer
git clone -b scarthgap git://git.yoctoproject.org/meta-raspberrypi poky/meta-raspberrypi

# Clone OpenEmbedded Extended Layers
git clone -b scarthgap git://git.openembedded.org/meta-openembedded poky/meta-openembedded
```

Directory layout:
```text
~/rpi-yocto/
└── poky/
    ├── bitbake/
    ├── meta/
    ├── meta-poky/
    ├── meta-raspberrypi/
    └── meta-openembedded/
        ├── meta-oe/
        ├── meta-python/
        └── meta-networking/
```

