## 7. Image Flashing & Storage Setup

Upon compilation completion, the deployment artifacts reside in:
`~/rpi-yocto/build/tmp/deploy/images/raspberrypi2/`

### 7.1 Key Generated Artifacts
- **WIC Disk Image:** `core-image-minimal-raspberrypi2.rootfs.wic.bz2` (or `.wic.zst`)
- **Block Map File:** `core-image-minimal-raspberrypi2.rootfs.wic.bmap`
- **Linux Kernel:** `kernel7.img` (ZImage wrapper for ARMv7)
- **Base Device Tree:** `bcm2709-rpi-2-b.dtb`
- **Bootloader Files:** `bootcode.bin`, `start.elf`, `fixup.dat`, `config.txt`, `cmdline.txt`

### 7.2 Flashing with `bmaptool` (Fast & Safe)
`bmaptool` writes only allocated disk blocks, flashing up to 5x faster than standard raw block copiers:

```bash
cd ~/rpi-yocto/build/tmp/deploy/images/raspberrypi2/

# Identify your MicroSD drive (e.g., /dev/sdb or /dev/mmcblk0)
lsblk

# Flash image (replace /dev/sdX with your actual block device)
sudo bmaptool copy core-image-minimal-raspberrypi2.rootfs.wic.bz2 /dev/sdX
```

### 7.3 SD Card Partition Layout
The `.wic` image automatically structures the SD card into two partitions:

```text
+-----------------------+---------------------------------------------+
| Partition 1: Boot     | Partition 2: RootFS                         |
| File System: FAT32    | File System: ext4                           |
| Label: boot           | Label: rootfs                               |
| Files:                | Files:                                      |
|  - bootcode.bin       |  - /bin, /sbin, /usr, /lib                  |
|  - start.elf          |  - /etc (systemd configuration)             |
|  - bcm2709-rpi-2-b.dtb|  - /dev, /proc, /sys (mount targets)        |
|  - kernel7.img        |  - /home/root                               |
|  - config.txt         |                                             |
|  - cmdline.txt        |                                             |
+-----------------------+---------------------------------------------+
```

